pose\",\"custom-alphabet-decode\",\"asset-cipher-dex-loader\",\"native-init-array-decrypt\",\n \"resource-id-const-resolve\",\"messagedigest-derived-answer\",\"v1-manifest-digest-verify\",\"dex-slack-and-header-anomaly\",\"aab-proto-manifest-parse\"}\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g[\"id\"] not in built]\nfor g in gaps:\n    if g[\"id\"]==\"identifier-collision-resolve\": g[\"priority\"]=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"rolling-xor-keystream-family\",\"concept\":\"position/rolling-key XOR string decryption (row 70; D18 TT `decryptByte`)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 shipped single-byte xor; its TT dex added a per-byte `decryptByte` helper, so the next escalation is a key that varies by index. Pure python over puzzle `data` (raw, b64, hex) and dex byte/char arrays: solve each family's parameters from the 4-byte known plaintext `ANS-` then verify the full `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`: c^(k+i), c^k^i, c^(k*i), (c-k-i)&0xff, c^key[i % n] with key from `key` (int/str/list) or dex strings, c^prev (cipher-feedback chaining, IV = key), c^lcg(seed) for Java Random / (a*x+c) mod 2^n with seeds from the JSON/dex, rotl/rotr by k then xor. Wire into puzzle_candidates' unknown-codec and xor-mismatch branches; <50 ms.\"},\n {\"id\":\"decrypt-call-site-args-eval\",\"concept\":\"evaluate a dex string-decrypt helper with the constant ARGS of each call site (rows 35, 70)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"dex_eval_scan runs methods with params \\\"\\\"/0, so `decrypt(\\\"<cipher>\\\", 7)` style helpers return garbage. Pure python on the existing mini interpreter: find every invoke-static/-virtual of an in-dex method whose return is String/[B/[C (or whose name contains decrypt/deobf/decode/xor, incl. renamed 1-letter ones with xor-int in the body), recover the caller's constant arguments (const-string, const ints, fill-array-data, sget of <clinit>-initialised fields) and run the callee with them; regex every result; return candidates for proof_flow ranking. Also run each helper over every const-string / array in the dex as a fallback.\"},\n {\"id\":\"known-string-obfuscator-signatures\",\"concept\":\"re-implement common open-source Android string obfuscators (row 71)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Detect by class/package names in the dex and decode statically: StringFog (`com/github/megatronking/stringfog`; default XOR of base64(data) with a key string passed at the call site, also the AES/Base64 variants), Paranoid (`io/michaelrocks/paranoid/Deobfuscator$...getString(long id)`: chunked string table + keystream from the id), obfuscapk EncryptStrings (AES-128-ECB, key a 32-hex dex const, hex ciphertext) and simple Allatori-style `ALLATORIxDEMO` char-xor loops. Return decoded strings to the ANS regex and proof_flow ranking; pure python + pycryptodome.\"},\n {\"id\":\"opaque-predicate-dead-branch\",\"concept\":\"opaque predicates and unreachable decoy literals (row 72)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Resilience days pair obfuscation with decoys. Pure python over dex code: constant-fold if-* conditions whose operands are consts or classic opaque forms (x*(x+1)%2==0, (x*x)%4 in {0,1}, x|~x, 7*y*y-1 != x*x) and mark basic blocks unreachable; demote `ANS-` candidates that only occur in dead blocks or uncalled methods, promote ones on the live path into `proof=`. Feed as a rank hint to proof_flow_scan.\"},\n {\"id\":\"java-serialized-object-parse\",\"concept\":\"Java serialization stream / Parcel blob in assets or dex arrays (row 73)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Pure python minimal ObjectInputStream grammar (magic AC ED 00 05: TC_OBJECT/TC_CLASSDESC/TC_STRING/TC_LONGSTRING/TC_ARRAY/TC_BLOCKDATA, field descriptors, primitive values) emitting every string + field name/value; fall back to scanning TC_STRING (0x74 + u16 len) records. Apply to any asset/raw entry or dex byte array with that magic (also base64/hex-wrapped); hand strings to decode_any and the ANS regex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jwt-token-decode-verify\",\"concept\":\"JWT / bearer tokens shipped in the app (row 74, MASVS-AUTH)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Scan dex/arsc/assets/.so strings for `eyJ...` three-part tokens: b64url-decode header + payload, list claims (ANS- may be a claim or kid), flag alg none, and verify HS256/384/512 with every dex/asset string as the key (cap ~2k) to report which key signs it. Also decode JWE headers. Pure python hmac/hashlib; candidates only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"protobuf-asset-wire-decode\",\"concept\":\"schema-less protobuf assets (row 75)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Generalise the AAB proto reader: for any asset/raw entry (or b64/hex blob) that parses fully as protobuf wire format, walk it recursively (LEN fields tried as nested message first, then UTF-8 string, then bytes), emitting field paths + string values to the ANS regex and decode_any. Guard against false positives by requiring full consumption and depth <= 8.\"},\n {\"id\":\"sqlcipher-asset-decrypt\",\"concept\":\"SQLCipher-encrypted asset database (row 76)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"When an assets/*.db lacks the `SQLite format 3` header and the dex references net/sqlcipher or a .so named libsqlcipher: try passwords from dex/arsc strings with SQLCipher 3/4 defaults (salt = first 16 bytes; PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA1 64000 iters (v3) / HMAC-SHA512 256000 (v4); AES-256-CBC per 1024/4096-byte page with the IV at the page tail), rebuild a plain image and pass it to the existing sqlite row scan. pycryptodome + hashlib; cap passwords at ~20 for the time budget.\"},\n]\nout=[]\nfor pr in (1,2,3):\n    out+= [g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==pr]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==pr]\nout=[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==1]+[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==1]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==2 and g[\"action\"]==\"prebuild\"]+[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==2]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==2 and g[\"action\"]!=\"prebuild\"]+[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==3]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==3]\nassert len(out)==len(gaps)+len(new)\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+\"\\n]\"\ns=s[:i]+body+s[j:]\nrep(\"\"\"apk-signing-block-payload, zip-structure-anomaly-scan, integrity-derived-key.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"apk-signing-block-payload, zip-structure-anomaly-scan, integrity-derived-key, ans-prefix-numeric-compose,\ncustom-alphabet-decode, asset-cipher-dex-loader, native-init-array-decrypt, resource-id-const-resolve,\nmessagedigest-derived-answer, v1-manifest-digest-verify, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly, aab-proto-manifest-parse.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\npython3 -I - <<'E'\nimport json\ns=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md').read()\ni=s.index(\"```json\\n\")+8; j=s.index(\"\\n```\",i)\ng=json.loads(s[i:j]); print(len(g)); [print(x['priority'],x['action'],x['id']) for x in g]\na=s.index(\"## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\"); b=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); print('cue lines', s[a:b].count('\\n'))\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":833,"cache_read_input_tokens":92072,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":833},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ac0157f-4942-470c-97f2-0b3e1d481171","uuid":"9697aa95-3da7-492d-961e-999f22205798","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:05:26.782Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9kTKgzsaHUFkyY8WGLa","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017J2sFLk8GSxnaydK8SGqss":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a