h a key string passed at the call site, also the AES/Base64 variants), Paranoid (`io/michaelrocks/paranoid/Deobfuscator$...getString(long id)`: chunked string table + keystream from the id), obfuscapk EncryptStrings (AES-128-ECB, key a 32-hex dex const, hex ciphertext) and simple Allatori-style `ALLATORIxDEMO` char-xor loops. Return decoded strings to the ANS regex and proof_flow ranking; pure python + pycryptodome.\"},\n {\"id\":\"opaque-predicate-dead-branch\",\"concept\":\"opaque predicates and unreachable decoy literals (row 72)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Resilience days pair obfuscation with decoys. Pure python over dex code: constant-fold if-* conditions whose operands are consts or classic opaque forms (x*(x+1)%2==0, (x*x)%4 in {0,1}, x|~x, 7*y*y-1 != x*x) and mark basic blocks unreachable; demote `ANS-` candidates that only occur in dead blocks or uncalled methods, promote ones on the live path into `proof=`. Feed as a rank hint to proof_flow_scan.\"},\n {\"id\":\"java-serialized-object-parse\",\"concept\":\"Java serialization stream / Parcel blob in assets or dex arrays (row 73)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Pure python minimal ObjectInputStream grammar (magic AC ED 00 05: TC_OBJECT/TC_CLASSDESC/TC_STRING/TC_LONGSTRING/TC_ARRAY/TC_BLOCKDATA, field descriptors, primitive values) emitting every string + field name/value; fall back to scanning TC_STRING (0x74 + u16 len) records. Apply to any asset/raw entry or dex byte array with that magic (also base64/hex-wrapped); hand strings to decode_any and the ANS regex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jwt-token-decode-verify\",\"concept\":\"JWT / bearer tokens shipped in the app (row 74, MASVS-AUTH)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Scan dex/arsc/assets/.so strings for `eyJ...` three-part tokens: b64url-decode header + payload, list claims (ANS- may be a claim or kid), flag alg none, and verify HS256/384/512 with every dex/asset string as the key (cap ~2k) to report which key signs it. Also decode JWE headers. Pure python hmac/hashlib; candidates only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"protobuf-asset-wire-decode\",\"concept\":\"schema-less protobuf assets (row 75)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Generalise the AAB proto reader: for any asset/raw entry (or b64/hex blob) that parses fully as protobuf wire format, walk it recursively (LEN fields tried as nested message first, then UTF-8 string, then bytes), emitting field paths + string values to the ANS regex and decode_any. Guard against false positives by requiring full consumption and depth <= 8.\"},\n {\"id\":\"sqlcipher-asset-decrypt\",\"concept\":\"SQLCipher-encrypted asset database (row 76)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"When an assets/*.db lacks the `SQLite format 3` header and the dex references net/sqlcipher or a .so named libsqlcipher: try passwords from dex/arsc strings with SQLCipher 3/4 defaults (salt = first 16 bytes; PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA1 64000 iters (v3) / HMAC-SHA512 256000 (v4); AES-256-CBC per 1024/4096-byte page with the IV at the page tail), rebuild a plain image and pass it to the existing sqlite row scan. pycryptodome + hashlib; cap passwords at ~20 for the time budget.\"},\n]\nout=[]\nfor pr in (1,2,3):\n    out+= [g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==pr]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==pr]\nout=[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==1]+[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==1]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==2 and g[\"action\"]==\"prebuild\"]+[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==2]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==2 and g[\"action\"]!=\"prebuild\"]+[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==3]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==3]\nassert len(out)==len(gaps)+len(new)\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+\"\\n]\"\ns=s[:i]+body+s[j:]\nrep(\"\"\"apk-signing-block-payload, zip-structure-anomaly-scan, integrity-derived-key.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"apk-signing-block-payload, zip-structure-anomaly-sc